{
  "campaign": "typical-dbsat-v1",
  "interpretations": [
    "Mixed/uncertain 'partial DB evidence' (\u00a76.3) = a pool signal with no \u00a76.2 pressure while (i) db_timeout > 0.1% is present (unattributed timeout) or (ii) at least one \u00a76.2 input is not assessable. No new numeric threshold is introduced.",
    "'Same type' of DB pressure in confirmation (\u00a77.4c) = the confirmation pressure types intersect the types that held in both discovery reps.",
    "A \u00a76.2/\u00a76.3 input that is not assessable (\u00a76.0 missing-minute rule) never satisfies a threshold; a step whose headroom is not assessable cannot serve as S*.",
    "When a candidate exists, a lower non-improving step that failed on headroom/pressure is listed as an observation; the candidate is the outcome.",
    "Performance Insights wait-event type names are matched case-insensitively (the API returns e.g. 'io', 'CPU', 'lock').",
    "Error rates by class use the steady-window denominator: each class's share of whole-step classified failures times steady failures / steady requests, because the adapter reports class counts for the whole step only.",
    "An overload (partial) step's window starts at the steady start floored to the minute and spans the observed steady minutes, matching the adapter's whole-minute perMinute rows.",
    "Achieved RPS of an overload (partial) step = steady requests / actual elapsed steady seconds, truncated last minute included: k6 steady-phase first-to-last request span when the raw k6 output is supplied, otherwise steady start to the recorded stop time (approximate; k6 graceful stop runs past it). Complete steps keep the 900 s steady window.",
    "Error rates by class, when the raw k6 output is supplied, come from the k6 request_outcomes points of the steady phase: class = the app error_class tag, or 'unclassified' when it is 'none'/missing on a status >= 400 or 0; rate = class count / steady request_outcomes points. Without the raw k6 output (or without request_outcomes points) the adapter's errorCategories are used as before. The source is recorded in error_classes_source."
  ],
